---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
---

<Layout title="Astro comparison — implementation status | OpenStack">
  <main id="main" class="status">
    <h1>OpenStack.org: Astro comparison</h1>
    <p>
      This independent implementation uses the committed SvelteKit beta content from September 12,
      2026. It is a framework comparison, not a replacement for production.
    </p>
    <h2>Native Astro</h2>
    <p>
      The homepage, AI and VMware marketing pages, software overview and release pages, navigation, footer and basic editorial templates render as HTML. The software
      catalogue is a direct React island: Astro renders its initial HTML and hydrates only the
      interactive application.
    </p>
    <h2>Shared content and media</h2>
    <p>
      Git-managed content and the approved media registry are copied from SvelteKit commit 032a176.
      Media is served from the same private R2 bucket through this site's own protected hostname. No
      pages are proxied from SilverStripe or SvelteKit.
    </p>
    <h2 id="authentication">Authentication and editing</h2>
    <p>
      Reviewer access is separate from application sign-in. OpenStackID callbacks and a separate
      GitHub CMS integration must be configured for this hostname before login or publishing is
      enabled. The software dataset remains a development snapshot.
    </p>
    <h2>Still being ported</h2>
    <p>
      Specialized interactive pages and structured summit templates are tracked separately. A notice
      means that this Astro template is not ready; it does not mean the existing SvelteKit migration
      is missing.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://beta.openstack.org/">Browse the SvelteKit beta ↗</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/software/">Try the React catalogue</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
<style>
  .status {
    max-width: 960px;
    margin: 48px auto;
    padding: 0 24px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  h1,
  h2 {
    color: #004976;
  }
</style>
